   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Morocco - Sustainable Post-Earthquake Debris Management Project to protect public health and the environment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">The earthquake of 8 September 2023, the most powerful to hit Morocco in a century, caused significant destruction, generating massive amounts of debris that need urgent, environmentally sound management to protect public health and the environment. The project aims to support the sustainable management of earthquake debris in the Provinces of El Haouz and Marrakech. Key activities include mapping debris locations, developing a debris management strategy that integrates climate resilience, and im</narrative>
  </description>
